,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Whzih","user":{"login":"matheusmdx","id":44306054,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzA2MDU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44306054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx","html_url":"https://github.com/matheusmdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-08T06:28:52Z","updated_at":"2024-12-08T06:28:52Z","body":"This is a regression, after unfocus the node that should auto-fold but that's broken right now.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2525444257/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2561825011","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100152#issuecomment-2561825011","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100152","id":2561825011,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Ysljz","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-25T10:30:59Z","updated_at":"2024-12-25T10:30:59Z","body":"> after unfocus the node that should auto-fold but that's broken right now.\n\nIt's not that simple. Making it fold brings back #81481\nRelevant code:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/0f95e9f8e665cedaa5aace5f6f86de2b4b5a8c60/editor/editor_properties.cpp#L3387-L3393","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2561825011/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3856647693","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100152#issuecomment-3856647693","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100152","id":3856647693,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7l38YN","user":{"login":"nearlytobias","id":65813194,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1ODEzMTk0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65813194?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias","html_url":"https://github.com/nearlytobias","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-05T22:24:17Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T22:24:17Z","body":"Since 4.6 this behaviour has been causing alot of friction while working in the built in script editor. Every time I click a node with an expanded Material, the shader editor opens itself and hijacks input focus. This moves the caret from the script editor to the shader code without user intervention, leading to accidental code entry in the wrong file. I thought leaving the shader editor open might help, but it will still highjack input focus.\n\nI'm often clicking around the scene tree to check properties while writing scripts and use a lot of materials, so it's a pain to manually have to close the shader editor repeatedly when I'm trying to focus on writing a script.  I've just opened my current project in 4.5.1 and this behaviour doesn't appear to be present in this context.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3856647693/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3934608664","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100152#issuecomment-3934608664","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100152","id":3934608664,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qhV0Y","user":{"login":"SirLich","id":18729296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NzI5Mjk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18729296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich","html_url":"https://github.com/SirLich","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-20T13:28:30Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T13:28:30Z","body":"Please note that focus will be stolen, even in the case where the user is inputing a search term in the inspector (for example: to find the material and close it ;))\n\nExample flow:\n- Click on the search field to focus\n- Begin typing\n- First letter will appear in search (e.g., `m`)\n- Remaining letters will appear in the open material (e.g., `aterial`)\n\nIt is only possible to search after closing the material resource. Otherwise focus will continue to be stolen.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3934608664/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4137269123","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100152#issuecomment-4137269123","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100152","id":4137269123,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72mbeD","user":{"login":"CSLRDoesntGameDev","id":126827743,"node_id":"U_kgDOB4883w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/126827743?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CSLRDoesntGameDev","html_url":"https://github.com/CSLRDoesntGameDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CSLRDoesntGameDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CSLRDoesntGameDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CSLRDoesntGameDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CSLRDoesntGameDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CSLRDoesntGameDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CSLRDoesntGameDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CSLRDoesntGameDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CSLRDoesntGameDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CSLRDoesntGameDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T18:26:49Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T18:26:49Z","body":"I'm popping in here since I've both been running into the issue a lot myself and attempting to fix it and this behavior gets weirder, maybe my insight would help..?\n\nthis doesn't happen if the shader editor is closed, in that scenario it pops up but doesnt steal focus. what i found is you can open the context menu on the node then close it, that gives focus to the node without opening the shader editor. _however_ if you click on another node then use the arrow keys to navigate up, the shader editor still opens.\n\nI've tried a few things but those have all failed or caused the shader editor dock to not pop up from other sources, which is a pretty big problem. i've just grown to live with it until someone finds a fix.","author_as